ed with this or not.\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **Preferences & UI Changes:**\n  - Demanded the total removal of the \"Tổng quan\" and \"Kiến trúc mục tiêu\" pages/tabs. Only \"Hiện trạng\" and \"Lộ trình\" remain.\n  - Loved the \"Segmented Control\" (Pill-shaped toggle) UI replacing the standard navigation bar to switch between the 2 remaining modules.\n  - Wanted ALL columns from their massive Excel files imported and displayed, without truncation.\n- **Architecture & Workflow:**\n  - Believes strongly in cross-linking systems. If a system in \"Hiện trạng\" needs an upgrade, there MUST be an associated task in \"Lộ trình\". \n- **Collaboration Context:**\n  - The user is working across two machines. They recently pulled their own changes from GitHub which included documentation (`HUONG_DAN_VA_LOGIC_HE_THONG.md`), utility scripts (`check_link.js`, `export_chat_history.js`), and a brand new feature they started: `src/app/(portal)/kts/so-do/page.tsx` (Diagram/Map).\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n- **UI Streamlined:** Completely deleted the `tong-quan` and `muc-tieu` folders. Redesigned `src/app/(portal)/layout.tsx` to use a modern, centered Ant Design `Segmented` control to toggle between \"Đánh giá Hiện trạng\" and \"Kế hoạch Lộ trình\".\n- **Database & Cross-Linking:** Added a Many-to-Many relation between `HeThongSo` and `NhiemVu` in `schema.prisma`. Updated API routes to handle nested writes (`connect`/`set`). \n- **Admin UI Upgraded:** Added a multiple-select dropdown in `admin/nhiem-vu/page.tsx` allowing users to link a task to multiple affected `HeThongSo` instances.\n- **Portal UI Upgraded:** `HienTrangPage` now dynamically displays all linked Tasks (with progress/deadlines) at the bottom of the system details popup. `LoTrinhPage` now shows blue tags indicating which systems are affected by a task.\n- **Data Import Fixed:** Rewrote `import_snn.js` to extract all 15+ columns from the Excel file (Frequency, Sharing format, Scopes) by packing them into the Prisma `moTa` string as `Key::Value\\n`. Fixed a major UI bug where internal Excel bullet points (newlines) were splitting improperly by ensuring the UI strictly splits by literal `/\\\\n/` instead of natural newlines.\n- **Git Sync:** Backed up the Gemini chat history to `.gemini_brain_backup` on Git, and then performed a `git pull` bringing down the user's laptop changes safely.\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Data Storage Hack:** Because the `HeThongSo` schema only has a generic `moTa` string, I packed Excel columns into it using the format `Key::Value\\n` (using the literal 2-character string `\\n`). The UI parser in `HienTrangPage` splits by `/\\\\n/` to render these as a table of `Descriptions.Item`. Do not use natural newlines for parsing, as Excel cell content often contains natural bulleted newlines.\n- **Prisma & Windows EPERM:** If you modify `schema.prisma` and run `db push`, you MUST kill the Next.js dev server first on this Windows machine. Otherwise, Next.js locks the Prisma query engine DLL, causing `EPERM` errors during generation.\n- **System Relationships:** The Prisma relation is named `HeThongNhiemVu` (implicit M-M). Access them via `heThongSos` (on `NhiemVu`) and `nhiemVus` (on `HeThongSo`).\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n**Thư mục làm việc chính:** `C:\\Delta Force\\kts-vinhlong`\n\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`:\n  - *Modified*: Added M-M relations `nhiemVus NhiemVu[]` and `heThongSos HeThongSo[]`.\n- `src/app/api/nhiem-vu/route.ts` & `src/app/api/nhiem-vu/[id]/route.ts`:\n  - *Modified*: Destructures `heThongSoIds` from payload and maps them to Prisma `connect` (POST) or `set` (PUT).\n- `src/app/admin/nhiem-vu/page.tsx`:\n  - *Modified*: Added `heThongSos` state, fetched systems in `Promise.all`, and added a multi-select field for `heThongSoIds`.\n- `src/app/(portal)/layout.tsx`:\n  - *Modified*: Replaced the top white secondary navbar with a sleek, centered `Segmented` control that pushes router paths to `/kts/hien-trang` and `/kts/lo-trinh`.\n- `src/app/(portal)/kts/hien-trang/page.tsx`:\n  - *Modified*: Improved `moTa` parsing logic to `rawMoTa.split(/\\\\n/)`. Added a UI section inside `renderModalContent` to display `selectedItem.nhiemVus`.\n- `src/app/(portal)/kts/lo-trinh/page.tsx`:\n  - *Modified*: Added small blue tags inside the Task column rendering `rec.heThongSos`.\n- `import_snn.js`:\n  - *Modified*: Replaced the truncated extraction logic with full `Key::Value\\n` construction.\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n**Immediate Context:**\nThe user's manager sent an image of an \"Overall Executive Dashboard\" for the Science & Technology Department. The user just asked: *\"nhưng hình trên có phải là Khung Kiến trúc Số của tỉnh theo quyết định ko\"* (But is the image above the Digital Architecture Framework of the province according to the decision?).\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1. **Answer the question:** Reply immediately to clarify that the image is **NOT** the Khung KTS. It is a general departmental dashboard. Khung KTS is highly specific to IT infrastructure, shared data, software applications, and integration layers (the exact stuff we've been building).\n2. **Restart Next.js:** Because of the system restart, the local web server died. Run the tool `run_command` with `npm run dev` to get it back up for the user.\n3. **Inquire about next priorities:** Ask if they want us to build a KTS Dashboard mimicking that manager's image, OR if they want to jump into the new `so-do` (Diagram) feature they were apparently building on their laptop.\n\nYou have the 26 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1789831851459]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Lnog/.gemini/antigravity/brain/0c724d03-995b-41e5-b753-c6096ba91ae8/.user_uploaded/media_1789831851459.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T15:31:01Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1789917998341]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Lnog/.gemini/antigravity/brain/0c724d03-995b-41e5-b753-c6096ba91ae8/.user_uploaded/media_1789917998341.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-20T15:26:54Z\n\n[ARTIF